---
description: Prefer native semantic HTML over divs/spans with ARIA roles
alwaysApply: true
---

# Semantic HTML

Use **native HTML elements** for structure and interaction. Do not recreate
built-in semantics with `<div>` / `<span>` plus `role`, except for patterns
that have no native equivalent (e.g. custom combobox widgets).

## Do

| Need | Use |
| ---- | --- |
| Image (incl. error/placeholder) | `<img alt="…">` |
| Modal / dialog surface | `<dialog>` (see shared `Modal`) |
| Clickable action | `<button type="button">` |
| Navigation target | `<a href="…">` |
| Page sections | `<main>`, `<nav>`, `<header>`, `<footer>`, `<section>`, `<article>` |
| Headings | `<h1>`–`<h6>` (one logical level per outline) |
| Lists | `<ul>` / `<ol>` + `<li>` |
| Data tables | `<table>`, `<thead>`, `<tbody>`, `<tr>`, `<th>`, `<td>` |
| Forms | `<form>`, `<label>`, `<input>`, `<textarea>`, `<select>` |

## Do not

- `<div role="img" aria-label="…">` — use `<img alt="…">` (transparent/data-URI `src` is fine for placeholders).
- `<div role="dialog" aria-modal="true">` — use `<dialog>`.
- `<div role="button" tabIndex={0}>` — use `<button>`.
- `<div role="link">` — use `<a href="…">`.
- `<div role="heading" aria-level="…">` — use `<h1>`–`<h6>`.
- `<div role="list">` / `<div role="listitem">` — use list elements.

## When ARIA roles are OK

- **Live regions:** `role="alert"` / `role="status"` on error or status messages when not using a native live-region wrapper.
- **Composite widgets:** `role="combobox"`, `role="listbox"`, etc. on custom controls built from primitives (Radix/Base UI patterns).
- **Grouping:** `role="group"` when no fieldset/legend fits.

## Enforcement

SonarQube and `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y` flag role-based substitutes for native
elements. Prefer semantic tags first; add ARIA only to extend, not replace, HTML
semantics.
